          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Return to Spain</strong><br>\nAfter his release from captivity, Cervantes struggled to find a stable career. He worked in various government positions, which often led to financial difficulties and legal problems. This period of his life was marked by personal challenges but also provided material for his literary works.</p>\n\n<p><strong>First Writings</strong><br>\nCervantes began his writing career with plays and poems. Although his playwriting did not bring him much success, he published his first significant work, \"La Galatea,\" in 1585. This pastoral novel was moderately successful and established him as a promising writer.</p>\n\n<p><strong>\"Don Quixote\"</strong><br>\nCervantes's most famous work, \"Don Quixote,\" was published in two parts in 1605 and 1615. The novel tells the story of a man who becomes a knight after reading too many chivalric romances. It is considered one of the greatest works of fiction ever written and marks the birth of modern European literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
