          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Life and Death</strong><br>\nDespite the success of \"Don Quixote,\" Cervantes's later life was not affluent. He wrote several other works, but none achieved the same acclaim. He died in Madrid on April 23, 1616, the same day as William Shakespeare, according to the Gregorian calendar used in Spain at the time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Literary Contributions</strong><br>\nCervantes's works contributed significantly to the Spanish language and are considered some of the most important in Spanish literature. His writings play a critical role in shaping the Spanish literary canon and continue to be studied and enjoyed worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence and Legacy</strong><br>\nCervantes's influence extends beyond literature into the Spanish language, which is sometimes referred to as \"the language of Cervantes.\" \"Don Quixote\" has been translated into over 50 languages, and its themes and characters resonate with audiences centuries after its publication, reflecting the universal appeal of his storytelling.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
